        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بچھڑنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بچھڑنا — bichhaṛnā — \"to be separated\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "میلے میں بچہ ماں سے بچھڑ گیا۔ mele meṅ bachchā māṅ se bichhaṛ gayā. At the fair the child got separated from his mother."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (she …): وہ بچھڑ گئی, voh bichhaṛ gaī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بچھڑنا (bichhaṛnā) is inherited: CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin bichuṛnā, \"is separated\", under a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 11651). The person you lose takes سے: ماں سے بچھڑ گیا."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
